  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting vulnerable displaced populations in Kalemie and Nyemba through the provision of camp coordination and camp management services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to address critical sectoral and geographic gaps in Tanganyika province, particularly in Kalemie and Nyemba health zones. The project will support the provision of critical Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) services in sites hosting displaced populations to facilitate the delivery of immediate life-saving assistance and improve the living conditions of 6,000 vulnerable internally displaced persons (IDPs). Key outcomes include improved living conditions of displaced populations through critical site upgrades, improved access to lifesaving assistance and protection services through enhance information sharing and referrals, and strengthened community governance and participation and accountability mechanisms in IDPs sites. Attention will be paid to ensure address the needs and ensure the inclusion of vulnerable groups, including women, children, persons with disabilities, the elderly and other persons facing heighten vulnerabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
